{
  "title": "About PlugMan Plugin",
  "story": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "711902a2c7ee43eb",
      "text": "PlugMan is a plugin manager for Federated Wiki. It began life as an explicit clone of Ward Cunningham's [[Plugmatic]] plugin (v1.5.1) and keeps its markup and routes while growing new administration features."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2f538303a2750c3b",
      "text": "This plugin queries the origin server for information about installed plugins. Server administrators can install new or updated existing plugins from included inventories."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "725d380d0f4119c6",
      "text": "See [[PlugMan Browse]] also in the hamburger (\u2630) menu."
    },
    {
      "type": "plugman",
      "id": "aa516c1dac55e70b",
      "text": "NAME\nPAGES\nBUNDLED\nINSTALLED\nSERVICE"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "2d06e967877db124",
      "text": "# Markup"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "b6188808197e3b69",
      "text": "Markup lines may include a full plugin name or a keyword. Keywords select columns and column order for reporting properties of each plugin."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "48788863a76362b3",
      "text": "Say STATUS for a traffic light indicating install options."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "405b19fdcca54bb4",
      "text": "Say NAME for the plugin name, sans wiki-plugin- prefix."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "826eb0f7d761ce48",
      "text": "Say MENU for Factory menu category, blank if unlisted."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "565ef5763ec2cd95",
      "text": "Say PAGES for count of about pages, blank if none."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0887156a2681e9ae",
      "text": "Say SERVICE for months installed, blank if absent or core."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5065dfdf958ce3d9",
      "text": "Say BUNDLED for version in wiki, blank if not bundled."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1033c6eede13b0f9",
      "text": "Say INSTALLED for version now installed, blank if absent."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "856d733cdab8fd8e",
      "text": "Say PUBLISHED for version posted to npm, blank if none."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "698979e7fd5fce6e",
      "text": "If no columns are requested a default list will be provided. Both STATUS and PUBLISHED require slow queries of npm so these are avoided except when specific plugins are inventoried."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "332c5da9a77f5fb4",
      "text": "Say BROWSE to show the about page browsing menu."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "de8a0565948198d8",
      "text": "# Sections"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0315a858ae8a6314",
      "text": "A section keyword scopes the plugin lines that follow it. Say FARM and a domain to inspect and manage a remote farm over REST. Say PRIVATE to mark the plugins under it as private or localhost-only, so the sync tool leaves them off lists built for a public farm. Say LOCAL to return to the ordinary local scope."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "c20e6bf9f5636ddd",
      "text": "A plugin that is symlinked for development but has no npm release shows an \"unpublished\" badge \u2014 these are the plugins in the Not-Published set. A private plugin shows a lock."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "aa885e328893b9da",
      "text": "# Sync"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "80c77d6b524b1939",
      "text": "Say SYNC, optionally with a target domain, for a panel that merges plugin lists from several sources \u2014 this laptop, the Not-Published set, and each FARM named in the item \u2014 into a new list. Choose a target server and press Build: PlugMan opens a ghost page listing the merged plugins, which you prune and fork to save as that server's roster. Private plugins are left out when the target is a public farm and kept for localhost."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "601f24a8b01bec46",
      "text": "# The Key Door\n\nEvery admin route answers to the wiki's admin, as before, or to a caller presenting an `X-Api-Key` listed in this site's `status/api-keys.json`. The file maps a scope to secrets and each secret to a holder \u2014 `*` for every route, or one of `plugman.install`, `plugman.update`, `plugman.uninstall`, `plugman.restart`, `plugman.view`, `plugman.status`, `plugman.catalog`. The wiki never serves the status folder; on a file-synced farm the file arrives by the same pipe as the pages. A keyed call is logged with the holder's id and the package it touched. `GET /plugin/plugman/key.json` says whether the key you present is accepted here and for which scopes, naming the holder and never the secret; `ready` says whether the site offers a door at all."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "4588bb114b14943f",
      "text": "The same file, in the same shape, is read by the Farm Plugin for its mounted writes. The sharing is the format and not the code: neither plugin needs the other installed. On the laptop, `wiki-farm-key mint <site>` writes the file and keeps the secret in the Keychain, and `wiki-plugman update-all <site>` brings a farm's plugins current without a browser \u2014 see [[Farm Key Plan]]."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "69d2b6f107f29fe6",
      "text": "## Repositories\n\n[https://github.com/Hitchhikers-Guide-to-the-Galaxy/wiki-plugin-plugman GitHub: wiki-plugin-plugman]\n\n[https://www.npmjs.com/package/wiki-plugin-plugman npm: wiki-plugin-plugman]"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "b97294e60a0ef05d",
      "text": "## Security"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "07603616475c51ea",
      "text": "PlugMan's admin routes install npm packages and restart the server, so an administrator can run code on the host. Safe by default. See [[PlugMan Security]]."
    }
  ],
